claim.claim-text:
1. A system for dynamic spectrum utilization management in an electromagnetic environment comprising:
a network slice or a subnetwork, wherein the network slice or the subnetwork includes an edge computing layer; and
wherein the edge computing layer includes at least one data analysis engine;
wherein the edge computing layer further includes an inference engine;
wherein the at least one data analysis engine analyzes measured data from the electromagnetic environment to create analyzed data;
wherein the inference engine learns the electromagnetic environment and identifies relevant information for optimizing network resources from the analyzed data using statistical learning techniques and control theory;
wherein the edge computing layer is operable to use the analyzed data and the relevant information identified by the inference engine to minimize interference by improving the overall signal-to-noise-plus-interference ratio (SINR) of at least one signal in the electromagnetic environment;
wherein the edge computing layer is operable to determine a location of at least one user equipment (UE) device; and
wherein the edge computing layer includes procedures for migration and/or service continuity using edge computing host pre-allocation based on a predicted future location of the at least one UE device.

8. A method for dynamic spectrum utilization management in an electromagnetic environment comprising:
providing an edge computing layer in a network slice or a subnetwork;
wherein the edge computing layer includes a data analysis engine;
wherein the edge computing layer further includes an inference engine;
processing measured data from the electromagnetic environment using the data analysis engine to generate analyzed data;
applying the inference engine within the edge computing layer to the analyzed data and identifying relevant information for optimizing network resources; and
generating via the edge computing layer, data for optimizing the network resources based on the analyzed data and the relevant information identified by the inference engine;
wherein the inference engine utilizes statistical learning techniques and/or control theory to learn the electromagnetic environment and identify the relevant information;
receiving via a wireless network optimization application the data and utilizing the data to generate at least one radio access network (RAN) command; and
the at least one RAN command coordinating resource allocation between a central unit (CU) and a distributed unit (DU) for spectrum sharing.

14. A method for dynamic spectrum utilization management in an electromagnetic environment comprising:
providing an edge computing layer in a network slice or a subnetwork;
wherein the edge computing layer includes a data analysis engine;
wherein the edge computing layer further includes an inference engine;
processing measured data from the electromagnetic environment using the data analysis engine to generate analyzed data;
applying the inference engine within the edge computing layer to the analyzed data for identifying relevant information for optimizing network resources and learning the electromagnetic environment using statistical learning techniques and control theory;
generating via the edge computing layer, data for optimizing the network resources based on the analyzed data and the relevant information identified by the inference engine;
receiving via a wireless network optimization application the data and utilizing the data to generate at least one radio access network (RAN) command; and
the at least one RAN command coordinating resource allocation between a central unit (CU) and a distributed unit (DU) for spectrum sharing;
wherein the relevant information for optimizing network resources is required by a customer application to reach customer goals.
